there is an emerging conflict tonight  between the people who want to keep this  country safe  and the engineers who have developed the  machines to do that national security  correspondent Jennifer Griffin tells us  some of them no longer want to  participate the US military is  developing a fleet of drones known as  gremlins to swarm the battlefield it's  working on robotic tanks submarine  drones and ships that can deploy for  months without any humans on board now  after teaming up with Silicon Valley  it's facing a rebellion from high-tech  civilian engineers who don't want their  expertise used to develop artificial  intelligence that could be used to kill  the technology is going to take us right  up to the point where it will be  possible to take humans out of the kill  chain a dozen Google employees quit this  week after more than three thousand  signed a petition demanding the high  tech giant not partner with the Pentagon  on project maven a DoD program allowing  computers to replace humans to wade  through hours of drone video quote we  believe that Google should not be in the  business of war therefore we ask that  project maven be cancelled and that  Google draft publicized and enforce a  clear policy stating that neither Google  nor its contractors will ever build  warfare technology the Pentagon is  collecting so much data off of Thrones  they can't possibly put enough people on  these video feeds to actually watch them  all Paul Sciarra author of army of none  worked at the Pentagon from 2008 to 2013  he explains the culture gap between  Silicon Valley and the Defense  Department what happens when a Predator  drone has as much autonomy as a  self-driving car and how much autonomy  are we willing to cede to machines when  we're talking about life and death  decisions the Pentagon says human beings  will still select the targets but with  an artificial intelligence arms race  already underway the US military fears  being left behind  China has ordered its technology giants  to help it advance on the battlefield  rush  developing fleets of armed robots and  has deployed robotic tanks to Syria  Google's Eric Schmidt sits on the  Pentagon's defense innovation board and  google says project maven is for quote  non offensive purposes but the company  may still need to convince their  engineers Brett Jennifer Griffin at the  Pentagon Jennifer thank you
 

